From 651f157fcc4daf0f2881e227f80da47426500813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:38:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09280/11362] Tool-assisted induction works as REPAIR, not
 replacement: +0.054 for one extra pass

Paired against 13 already-recorded single-shot cells (same generator, prompt,
window and deterministic seeds), on six games:

  single-shot only            0.912 mean recall   13 passes
  tool loop standalone        0.558               13 passes   LOSES, W/T/L 2/4/7
  loop-first + fallback       0.966               13 + 8 extra
  repair mode (<0.6 gate)     0.966               13 + 1 extra

So the standalone loop is not the shipping form, and repair mode captures the
ENTIRE gain for a single extra induction.

WHY THAT WORKS: the loop's own mismatch trajectory is a perfect predictor of its
output. Converged (trajectory ends at 0), n=5 -> recall 1.000 every time. Not
converged, n=8 -> mean 0.282. Single-shot on those same five cells averaged 0.859,
so when the loop converges it BEATS single-shot. The gain concentrates in one cell:
sp80 t1, single-shot 0.294, loop 1.000 -- a sampling-collapse cell recovered. vc33
t0 also improved (+0.166) WITHOUT converging, so the <0.6 gate leaves some on the
table.

Repair mode routes the REQ-6410 recall-gated resample's re-draw through the tool
loop, seeded with the failed engine as candidate 0 so the keep rule stays monotone.
Two independent gates, both default OFF. 43 tests.

CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER RESULT IN THIS REPO'S HISTORY. A first A/B reported
"0.912 -> 0.330, tool loop fails decisively". That measurement was INVALID: the
harness monkeypatches a path calling generate() directly, while the tool-loop hook
lives in induce(), so the flag was dead and zero tool requests reached the server
(confirmed: max_raw_completion_len median 12,784 vs 185,786 for single-shot).

What it actually measured was CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_THINKING_BUDGET=3072, which
generate() does read. So that table is a clean paired measurement of the
thinking-budget lever, and it is a strong NEGATIVE: capping thinking to ~5% of the
usual budget costs -0.58 mean recall. That lever was wired in c80822a94d and ships
default OFF; this is the measurement saying leave it off. It also corroborates
exp6221's finding that thinking helps held-out accuracy.

The error is worth recording because an earlier brief in this session warned
against exactly it -- "a lever that never fires produces a clean, zero-error NULL
that looks like a finding and is a bug" -- and the check that would have caught it
before reporting is one line: confirm the transport saw traffic.

ALSO IN THIS COMMIT

lp85 baseline refresh (operator-approved). Solve count held at 7; 39 per-game
reference numbers moved, the largest being lp85 efficiency 2.0069 -> 0.0039 (the
2026-08-07 frontier-tier trade this refresh exists to record) alongside genuine
improvements from the O(n^2) fix -- m0r0 0.0002 -> 0.0008, another game
0.0264 -> 0.0661, median actions on core 7805 -> 1661. This clears the last gate
blocker; the pre-refresh copy was preserved and diffed rather than overwritten
silently.

13 freshness acknowledgements refiled, each naming the exact hash, reason and
